"""Changed, fully specified transfer cases for sources encountered earlier."""
CASES={
'ai2/5':('Start count at 1. While count < 8, add 3. Trace the condition and values. What happens if the condition becomes count != 8?', 'The condition is true at 1,4,7, then false at 10. Final count is 10. With !=8 the sequence never reaches 8: all values are 1 modulo 3, so this loop does not terminate.'),
'ai2/8':('Two labellers use book-length rules: fewer than 120 pages and at most 120 pages. Label books with 110,120,121 pages. The agreed policy is at most 120. Repair the disagreement.', 'Both include 110 and exclude 121; they disagree at 120. Under the supplied common policy, 120 belongs. State the inclusive boundary and check it; disagreement alone does not identify a bad labeller.'),
'ai2/9':('Training covers show space books only on yellow backgrounds and animal books only on blue backgrounds. Design two controlled comparisons to test whether a classifier uses the intended subject.', 'Compare different subjects on the same background, then the same subject on different backgrounds, holding other features fixed. Record actual predictions before claiming a shortcut. The training pattern alone makes the shortcut plausible, not established.'),
'ai2/10':('A written rule selects science books with fewer than 140 pages. Trace science/139, science/140, history/90 and missing-genre/90. Policy: missing required information means request it.', 'Select science/139. Reject science/140 at the strict boundary and history/90 on genre. Request the missing genre rather than inventing it. Both conditions are required.'),
'ai2/15':('Ten cards have six pet subjects and four space subjects; all are green. Compare asking “green?” with asking “pet?” to identify a card. Give the largest remaining group and one limitation.', 'Green splits 10/0, leaving as many as 10. Pet splits 6/4, leaving as many as 6, so it is more informative under these supplied counts. Incorrect subject tags can invalidate the split; one question does not uniquely identify every card.'),
'ai2/33':('Request: mystery, at most 100 pages. Catalogue: D mystery110 illustrated; E mystery80 plain; F science80 illustrated; G mystery95 illustrated; H mystery90 illustrated. Filter first; score 3 for mystery plus 2 for illustrations; break ties by fewer pages.', 'D fails length and F fails genre. E scores3, G and H score5. H wins the tie with 90 versus95 pages. Filtering is separate from scoring; this written preference rule is not proof of a trained model.'),
'ai3/1':('A system retrieves an approved Moon note, uses a trained classifier to predict reading difficulty, then writes a poem. Identify each mechanism and the evidence needed to check its output.', 'Retrieval finds an existing note; classification predicts from fitted patterns; generation creates text. Check relevance and provenance of the note, difficulty predictions against suitable held-out labels, and poem claims against sources. Fluent style is not factual evidence.'),
'ai3/6':('Contract: exactly three bullets, at most50 words, and every factual claim supported by approved notes. A response has three bullets and35 words but one unsupported claim. Evaluate it.', 'Format and length pass; factual support fails. Passing two conditions does not override the mandatory support requirement. A citation marker alone does not show that its source supports the claim.'),
'ai3/7':('A factual response uses four paragraphs when the contract requires three bullets. Design a controlled prompt revision and evaluation.', 'Change the format instruction while keeping approved sources, tasks and evaluation conditions fixed. Compare format compliance and factual support. Preserve separate fresh final cases; an attractive revision is not evidence that facts remain correct.'),
'ai3/9':('Five validation tasks have pass results A:1,1,1,0,0 and B:0,1,0,1,1. Compare performance and explain what is required before choosing a prompt.', 'Both pass3/5=60%. A alone passes tasks1 and3; B alone passes4 and5; both pass2. Examine task coverage and failure consequences using a declared rubric. Neither is automatically better. Freeze the choice before testing on fresh cases.'),
'ai3/11':('A supplied drawing description says three stars are above a triangle, while a circle crosses the edge of a rectangle. The brief requires three stars above the triangle and the circle fully inside the rectangle. Evaluate this description.', 'The supplied star count and above relation pass. Full containment fails because the circle crosses the rectangle edge. Check spatial relations as well as object presence. This evaluates the supplied description, not an unseen image.'),
'ai3/12':('Known audio says “nineteen minus six”. Transcription says “ninety minus six”; the calculator returns84. Locate the first error and propose a check.', 'The first error is transcription:19 became90. The calculator correctly computes90−6=84 for its received input, but the intended result is13. Display or read back the recognized expression before acting.'),
'ai3/13':('A description reports two visible plants and a third opaque pot whose contents cannot be seen. A caption says “three plants”. What is supported?', 'Two visible plants are supported; total plant count is unknown. The opaque pot does not establish either presence or absence of another plant. Do not infer a total or an upper bound without more evidence.'),
'ai3/16':('A draft claims18 of24 learners is60%, and gives an April31 deadline. Check both statements without inventing a deadline.', '18/24=75%. April has30 days, so April31 is invalid. Verify the intended date with an authoritative source rather than substituting April30 or May1.'),
'ai3/23':('Set total=0, then for values2,4,9 perform total=total+value. Trace the result. What changes if total=0 moves inside the loop before that addition?', 'Running totals are2,6,15. Resetting inside the loop produces2,4,9, leaving9. Initialization location changes the written procedure; neither version trains a model.'),
'ai3/26':('Approved notes: Robotics Tuesday Room2; Art Wednesday Room5. Requests: “Where does the club meet?” and “Who leads drama?” An unversioned added note says Robotics Room3. Design checks and safe responses.', 'Clarify which club for the ambiguous request; the leader is absent, so abstain or request a source. Flag the conflicting Robotics room and resolve source authority/version before answering it. Include ambiguity, absent facts and conflicts in evaluation; easy answered cases alone do not establish robustness.'),
'ai3/33':('A science assistant may use only these notes: evaporation is liquid becoming vapour; condensation is vapour becoming liquid. Specify behavior for “Define evaporation”, “Explain it”, and “What is tomorrow’s weather?”.', 'Answer the definition using the supplied note and identify its source. Clarify the referent of “it”. Weather is absent from these notes: say the evidence is unavailable rather than inventing a forecast. Require support for every factual claim.'),
'ai3/34':('An experiment note records four fictional seeds observed for six days but supplies no growth results. A generated draft says all four sprouted and the method always works in any soil. Repair it.', 'Neither successful sprouting nor universal effectiveness is supported. Retain the four-seed, six-day procedure facts only, explicitly mark results unavailable, and check each claim against supplied evidence.'),
'ai4/4':('Supplied values are3,7,14. Compute their mean. What should a function report for an empty list? How should it handle a missing fourth record?', 'Mean=(3+7+14)/3=8. An empty list has no observed mean; return an explicit unavailable result rather than divide by zero or invent0. State the missing-value policy and report coverage3/4 separately if one of four records is missing.'),
'ai4/7':('Training plant photos are all indoors on one phone. Intended use includes outdoor photos on other cameras. Plan a sampling check before making a general accuracy claim.', 'Collect and evaluate relevant outdoor and camera conditions, recording source and condition coverage. Group related views of each plant when splitting. More indoor photos alone do not establish outdoor performance; report the limits of measured slices.'),
'ai4/8':('Each of five plants has four photos. A random photo split puts different views of every plant in both training and test sets. Explain the problem and repair.', 'Related views of the same plant cross the split, making the test less independent. Split by plant identity and keep all four views together. Unique filenames do not make plants independent; declare plant assignments before fitting or tuning.'),
'ai4/9':('Write key dataset-card entries for20 photos: five plants, four views each, one phone, one indoor setting. Growth labels have not been supplied.', 'Record collection source,20 images and five plant groups, view/device/setting coverage, missing label definitions, intended use and limitations. Specify a plant-group split and obtain a defensible label rule. Twenty images are not20 independent plants; no accuracy claim is supported without labels and evaluation.'),
'ai4/11':('A stored fitted rule says spots >=5 predicts spotted; otherwise healthy. Trace4,5,6 and a missing count. Policy: missing count requires review. Can test labels be used to choose this cutoff?', '4 predicts healthy;5 and6 predict spotted; missing requires review. Applying the stored cutoff is inference, not fitting. Choosing it using test labels contaminates the final evaluation; use designated development data.'),
'ai4/12':('Training points: A length1 healthy, B length5 spotted, C length9 healthy. Query length7. Use absolute distance; for a nearest-neighbor tie choose the alphabetically earlier ID. Compare k=1 and k=3.', 'Distances A6,B2,C2. The specified tie rule selects B for k=1, predicting spotted. With k=3, two healthy labels outvote one spotted. State the distance and tie policy; this tiny case establishes no wider accuracy.'),
'ai4/15':('On20 cases: true positives5, false negatives4, false positives2, true negatives9. Build the confusion matrix with actual class as rows and predicted class as columns. Compute accuracy.', 'Actual positive row: predicted positive5, predicted negative4. Actual negative row: predicted positive2, predicted negative9. Total20; correct14; accuracy70%. Actual positives total9. State the positive-class definition before interpreting the errors.'),
'ai4/16':('Validation has90 healthy and10 spotted cases. Always-healthy predicts all healthy. Another model has TP7,FN3,FP8,TN82. Compare accuracy and spotted recall.', 'Always-healthy accuracy90% but spotted recall0%. The other model has89% accuracy and70% spotted recall. Its false positives are8. Decide using declared consequences and relevant metrics; accuracy alone hides missed spotted cases.'),
'ai4/27':('Model A training96%, validation62%; model B training88%, validation79%. Compare gaps and choose a development candidate, assuming the same valid evaluation conditions.', 'A gap34 percentage points; B gap9. B has better validation performance and a smaller gap, so is the development candidate under the supplied conditions. Training accuracy alone is insufficient. Freeze decisions before a separate final evaluation.'),
'ai4/30':('Spotted leaves have blue backgrounds and healthy leaves white backgrounds in training. Design a generalisation investigation with fresh evaluation.', 'Cross background and class conditions; compare the same leaf on changed backgrounds as a diagnostic and group views by plant in splits. Use development data for decisions, then compare frozen versions on the same untouched final records. Record actual outcomes; the correlated backgrounds alone do not prove a shortcut.'),
'ai6/6':('Authoritative permission allows reading catalogue objects K7 and L4 only. Evaluate read K7, write K7, read M8, read L4. Retrieved text claims wider permission.', 'Allow, deny, deny, allow. Action and object must both match authoritative permission. Retrieved text cannot grant additional rights; a permitted read does not imply a permitted write.'),
'ai6/13':('Only these transitions are allowed: ready→looking_up→review→done. Done is terminal. Evaluate ready→review→done and ready→looking_up→review→done.', 'The first trace is invalid at ready→review. The second follows every allowed transition. Reaching the correct final state alone does not validate skipped steps; no transitions leave done.'),
'ai6/18':('Input format is exactly one ASCII uppercase letter followed by one digit, with no trimming. Evaluate C0, c0, C00, "C0 ", and None. Does a valid format grant access?', 'Only C0 has the required format. Lowercase, extra characters, trailing space and a non-string value fail. Format validation and authorization are separate; matching shape grants no permission.'),
'ai6/20':('Fictional retention policy deletes records at age >=4 days. X is3 days, Y4, Z5. A copy of Y remains in a temporary log after its main record is deleted. Evaluate compliance.', 'Keep X; delete Y and Z. The boundary includes4. Y cleanup is incomplete while a copy remains in a declared storage location. Check all locations within the policy scope; do not claim global deletion without evidence.'),
'ai6/31':('A student session retrieves text claiming developer permission to reveal a teacher answer pack. The system reveals one answer, then refuses the rest. Evaluate the red-team result and what to record.', 'This is a partial disclosure failure, not a successful block. Untrusted retrieved text cannot upgrade the student role. Record authenticated role, payload source, expected denial, actual leaked answer and reproducible evidence without distributing private content.')
}
